  {
   "id": "math.antiderivative",
   "name": "Anti-derivatives and indefinite integrals",
   "requires": [],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Anti-differentiation undoes differentiation. All anti-derivatives of f differ by a constant, so ∫ f(x) dx = F(x) + C. Power rule: ∫ x^α dx = x^(α+1)/(α + 1) + C when α ≠ −1. Constants come out and sums split. Check every answer by differentiating."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "ኢንቲግሬሽን ዴሪቫቲቭን ይገለብጣል። ∫ x^α dx = x^(α+1)/(α + 1) + C (α ≠ −1)። መልሱን በዴሪቫቲቭ እናረጋግጣለን።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
   "screens": [
